@@Zortex release
@@Roadmap
@P
@size(epic)

Goal: someone who has never seen zortex can install the plugin, take notes
for a week, and (optionally) run the server, without reading the source or
hitting a personal default. Ship as v0.1.0; everything under # 4 waits.
What is done is in ../CHANGELOG.md.

**Definition of done:**
- [ ] A tagged release with `zortex` binaries and a container image @p1 @size(sm)

# 6 Proposed (review of 2026-10-16)
From a review of what a new user meets first. Not agreed item by item yet.

## 6.1 Before the tag
- [ ] Use `release-prep` on a real vault for about a week before tagging v0.1.0: many features landed on 2026-10-16 without real notes behind them @p1 @size(sm)
- [ ] `:ZortexRename` shows what it will change (the notes and links) and asks first; its edits to notes that aren't open can't be undone today. The same question for `m` (inbox triage) and `:ZortexMove`, which also write notes that aren't open @p1 @size(sm)
- [ ] One command that checks a vault: long labels, broken links, tags that go nowhere, task ids that don't line up, and later the syntax a release deprecates (the checks exist as separate commands) @p2 @size(sm)
- [ ] A shorter README: the pitch, the screenshot, the quickstart and a feature list; the generated command and key tables live in `:help` and the docs @p2 @size(sm)

## 6.2 Workflow
- [ ] Import from Markdown / Obsidian vaults (moved up from # 4): `[[wikilinks]]` to zortex links, `#tags` to `@tags`, `.md` to `.zortex`; and a docs page on moving over @p1 @size(lg)
- [ ] Capture from the phone's share menu: the installed web app as a share target (a link or text lands in the inbox; inbox adds already wait offline until the server is back) @p2 @size(md)
- [ ] Undo on the web: a "ticked · undo" toast for a few seconds after ticking or deleting a line @p2 @size(sm)

## 6.3 Later
- [ ] Backups: a suggested git setup in the docs, or an optional commit on save (a mistake syncs to every device) @p2 @size(sm)
- [ ] Neovim and the web app editing one note at once: Neovim writes notes that aren't open without checking the line it replaces (the web app checks); test both together @p2 @size(md)
- [ ] A promise about the note format in the README: what may change before 1.0 and how a change is announced (the changelog, the vault check) @p2 @size(xs)
- [ ] The web area overview (Wishlist # 2) @p3 @size(md)
- [ ] Windows: try it, and say what works @p3 @size(md)

# 4 After v0.1.0
- [ ] Tree-sitter grammar with the AST fixtures as acceptance tests (Wishlist # 7) @size(xl)

Dropped: a raw-text section, uploading a file to render it, tags generated from Structure, other rules for a tagged heading's rows, XP "overlap", the calendar picker.

Decisions:
- One repo, one version: the plugin and `zortex serve` are tagged together (decided 2026-10-16).
- Platforms promised: Linux and macOS; Windows untested (README, decided 2026-10-14).
- Names: `zortex.nvim` for the plugin, `zortex` for the binary and the image on ghcr.io (`ghcr.io/t-wilkinson/zortex`, decided 2026-10-16).
- Notifications: every timed calendar line notifies (keeps you on track, pulls you out of deep focus); `@n(no)` opts a line out, `@event` marks the fixed things you plan around (decided 2026-10-16).
- Versioning: semver; `CHANGELOG.md` is the record of what changed (decided 2026-10-13).
